* Two-Stage CMOS Miller Operational Amplifier (Transistor-Level IC Netlist)
* Modeled after Texas Instruments TLC271 / LMC6041 Architecture
* Pinout: 1:IN+  2:IN-  3:VDD  4:VSS  5:OUT
.subckt CMOS_OPAMP 1 2 3 4 5

* Generic 0.5um / 180nm CMOS Transistor Models
.model NMOS NMOS (Level=1 Vto=0.7 Kp=120u Gamma=0.4 Lambda=0.02 Phi=0.7)
.model PMOS PMOS (Level=1 Vto=-0.7 Kp=50u Gamma=0.57 Lambda=0.03 Phi=0.8)

* --- Input Differential Stage ---
* M1, M2: NMOS Input Pair (1:IN+, 2:IN-)
M1 11 2 10 4 NMOS W=20u L=2u
M2 12 1 10 4 NMOS W=20u L=2u

* M3, M4: PMOS Active Current Mirror Load
M3 11 11 3 3 PMOS W=40u L=2u
M4 12 11 3 3 PMOS W=40u L=2u

* M5: Tail Current Source (40uA)
M5 10 14 4 4 NMOS W=40u L=2u

* --- Second Gain Stage ---
* M6: PMOS Common-Source Amplifier
M6 5 12 3 3 PMOS W=120u L=2u

* M7: NMOS Current Source Load (160uA)
M7 5 14 4 4 NMOS W=160u L=2u

* --- Miller Frequency Compensation ---
* Cc and nulling resistor Rz to eliminate RHP zero
Cc 12 13 3p
Rz 13 5 1.5k

* --- Bias Generation Network ---
* M8 establishes Vbias from reference current Iref
M8 14 14 4 4 NMOS W=40u L=2u
Iref 3 14 40u

.ends CMOS_OPAMP
